From: Copperline bundled-ROM refresh 2026-09-05
Subject: [PATCH] m68k-amiga/dos: keep the 8 KiB process stack floor

Commit e9c4ecde99 ("Reduce CD32 boot-time chip memory use") lowered the
m68k DOS process stack minimum from AROS_STACKSIZE (16 KiB) to 4 KiB and
pinned the Shell-seg, "Boot Mount" and lddemon processes at 4 KiB, sized
from a CD32 disc boot that runs no Startup-Sequence. A boot that does run
one -- a staged boot volume with a `Run`/`Execute` line and handler
processes for host-directory and hardfile mounts -- overflows those stacks:
the program never starts, the boot process later warm-reboots. Restoring
an 8 KiB floor (the "conservative default for arbitrary applications" the
same commit keeps as PROC_STACKSIZE) fixes it; raising the Shell-seg pin
alone, the bootstrap stack alone, or the handler's own request alone does
not.

Applied on top of upstream master a3cfa659ed for the bundled ROM.

--- a/arch/m68k-amiga/dos/dos_platform.h
+++ b/arch/m68k-amiga/dos/dos_platform.h
@@ -1,10 +1,11 @@
 #ifndef DOS_PLATFORM_H
 #define DOS_PLATFORM_H
 
-/* Amiga interrupts and exceptions use the supervisor stack.  Keep a
- * conservative default for arbitrary applications while allowing measured
- * system processes to request the classic 4 KiB process stack. */
+/* Amiga interrupts and exceptions use the supervisor stack.  Keep a
+ * conservative default for arbitrary applications and floor every process
+ * at it too: a Startup-Sequence boot with handler processes overflows the
+ * classic 4 KiB stack that a CD32 disc boot gets by with. */
 #define PROC_STACKSIZE     8192
-#define PROC_MINSTACKSIZE  4096
+#define PROC_MINSTACKSIZE  8192
 
 #endif
